    [
     1,
     "Hi Jia,\r<br>\r<br>Yes, it&#39;s a bug - <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/ggvis/issues/90\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/ggvis/issues/90&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485151295000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0eFjbbs-3q_H7z7y5KVddB\">https://github.com/rstudio/ggvis/issues/90</a>. I don&#39;t\r<br>think a fix should be too hard.\r<br>\r<br>Hadley\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Thu, Feb 27, 2014 at 1:29 PM, Jia Kang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ji...@metrumrg.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Firstly, big congrats to the release of ggvis 0.1.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Secondly, I have a question regarding properties in axis. The same question\r<br>&gt; was also mentioned before.\r<br>&gt; I used ggvis 0.1 and tried the code presented on the ggvis website\r<br>&gt; (<a href=\"http://ggvis.rstudio.com/axes-legends.html#custom-styles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ggvis.rstudio.com/axes-legends.html%23custom-styles&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485151295000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3mGlxjYvUgX2OkuOudLgDf\">http://ggvis.rstudio.com/axes-legends.html#custom-styles</a>)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ggvis(mtcars, props(x = ~wt, y = ~mpg)) +\r<br>&gt;   mark_symbol() +\r<br>&gt;   guide_axis(&quot;x&quot;, properties = list(\r<br>&gt;     axis = props(stroke = &quot;red&quot;, strokeWidth = 5),\r<br>&gt;     grid = props(stroke = &quot;blue&quot;),\r<br>&gt;     ticks = props(stroke = &quot;blue&quot;, strokeWidth = 2),\r<br>&gt;     labels = props(angle = 45, align = &quot;left&quot;, fontSize = 20)\r<br>&gt;   ))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I am not sure how the properties work on the axis. I thought in the\r<br>&gt; resulting picture, the x axis should be red and ticks on the x axis should\r<br>&gt; be blue. However, it&#39;s not. Do I miss something here?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Another question, after I make a plot using ggvis, is there any function\r<br>&gt; that allow me to get the javascript (html) code for the plot? It might be\r<br>&gt; helpful for checking the result from R code along with javascript code for\r<br>&gt; vega).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thanks.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
